herolte: the phone takes its own screenshots, with a gesture script (0484, S7UI lab)

The Director's description of the iPhone-style screen ("se ve raro, algunas cosas mal puestas, la barra de arriba no se ve", side bars, a Control Center that sometimes goes home) cannot be turned into a fix without seeing it. hsnap=<s> starts a thread that, <s> seconds after the power thread (the home screen is up), plays gestures through the real touch path (home, Control Center from the top right, Notification Center from the top left, the home swipe from the bottom edge, a page swipe, the home key) and after each step prints the panel buffer on show, one pixel in five each way (288x512), RGB565 in base64, one log line per row; tools/herolte-snap-decode.py rebuilds the PNGs from a pulled log. Reads only. Off by default; the 10 ms-per-line pacing keeps the log buffer from overflowing.

--- a/bsd/dev/herolte_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/herolte_gpu.c
